我们需要回答 15 题。需要独立求解。注意题目编号：9,10,V.1-V.8,VI.1-VI.5 共2+8+5=15。需要给标准答案和关键步骤。必须 JSON 代码块 only。让我们逐题分析。

9. Father often tells me ______ too much time on computer games.
A don't spend B not spend C not to spend D not spending
tell sb not to do sth. 所以 C。

10. As teenagers, we're old enough to ______ housework. We can help set the table, wash dishes and clean our own rooms.
A help B help with C help to D help to clean
help with housework 帮助做家务。old enough to help with housework. 所以 B。注意 "help with sth" 正确。A help housework 不对，C help to 不完整，D help to clean housework 不通。B。

V.1 He always provides a context that makes his characters ______ (believe). 词性？ believe 动词，make his characters believable? 这里需要形容词作宾补：believable。但是括号给 (believe)，通常变为 believable。句子：provides a context that makes his characters believable. 所以 believable。

V.2 She had thought very ______ (depth) about this problem. 需要副词修饰 thought: deeply. depth -> deeply。注意 "thought very deeply about". 所以 deeply。

V.3 There is little hope that they will be found ______ (life). 他们被找到活着？ found alive. 括号 (life) 应该变 alive。There is little hope that they will be found alive. 正确。

V.4 The staff is busy making ______ (prepare) for the new textbooks for students. make preparations for. 所以 preparations (复数)。staff 作整体？ "The staff is busy making preparations for..." 对。

V.5 All the tickets having been sold out, they went away ______ (disappoint). 他们离开，感到失望。副词修饰 went away? disappointed? 这里独立主格 All the tickets having been sold out, they went away disappointed. 形容词作主语补足语，表示状态。disappointed。也可能 disappointedly 副词修饰 went away，但 "went away disappointed" 更自然。括号 disappoint，填 disappointed。意思是失望地离开。如果副词 disappointedly 表示方式，也对？但英语中 go away disappointed 很常见。需要判断标准答案。句子：All the tickets having been sold out, they went away ______ (disappoint). 独立主格 + 主句。went away 后可接形容词作主补，disappointed。副词 disappointedly 也可但稍怪。填 disappointed。

V.6 I will meet you at one of the main ______ (enter). 主入口之一：entrances. main entrances. enter -> entrance，one of the main entrances 复数。所以 entrances。

V.7 The waiters threaded between the ______ (crowd) tables. 拥挤的桌子：crowded tables。crowd -> crowded 形容词。所以 crowded。

V.8 Graduates have to fight for jobs in a highly ______ (compete) market. 竞争激烈的市场：competitive. highly competitive. 所以 competitive。

VI.1 Mum's words rang in his head. (改为否定句) Mum's words ______ ______ in his head.
原句一般过去时 rang -> didn't ring. 所以 "didn't ring" 或 "did not ring"。两个空：didn't ring。但两个空是 "Mum's words ______ ______ in his head." 第一个空 did not? 第二个 ring? 原句 rang 是过去式，否定句用 didn't ring。如果两个空，可能第一空 did，第二空 not ring? 不对，每个空一个词？通常改写句子，两个空格，填 "didn't" "ring" 或者 "did" "not ring"？看格式 Mum's words ______ ______ in his head. 两个空，通常第一个填 didn't，第二个填 ring。但 didn't 是一个词。如果是两个空，可能 "did not" 和 "ring"？但只有两个空，所以 "didn't ring" 是两词，第一空 didn't，第二空 ring。答案：didn't ring. 步骤：一般过去时否定用 didn't + 动词原形。如果严格填两个空，可能 "did not" 分成两空？原句 "rang" 改否定：Mum's words didn't ring in his head. 两个空：didn't / ring。如果第一空写 didn't，第二空 ring。正确。

VI.2 He deals with the problem carefully. (改为现在完成时) He ______ ______ with the problem carefully.
